        },
        "markdown": "# 4 · Identity and Historical Context\n## 12:27–18:30\n\nLionel discusses Candace's position as a Black conservative and contrasts her with an older model of acceptable conservative dissent that stayed within permitted boundaries.\n\n**Editorial function:** widen the argument historically and culturally, then explain why the subject represents a category-breaking case. ",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
