        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study-moves",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Editorial Moves",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 60,
        "y": 340
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 430,
      "color": "linear-gradient(135deg,#3b0764,#6b21a8)",
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-episode-grammar-study-01"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🎙️ Editorial Moves\n\nThese are the **actions Lionel performs on the material**:\n\n- rejects a public characterization\n- names an underlying system\n- identifies a double standard\n- proposes institutional motives\n- introduces a supporting case\n- adds historical or cultural context\n- synthesizes the accumulated argument\n- issues instructions to the audience\n- performs the recurring show outro\n\nThis distinction is central: **objects answer what the episode discusses; moves answer what makes the episode structurally Lionel.**",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786052694504,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study-types",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Provisional Segment Types",
