      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-episode-grammar-study-01"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🏗️ Emerging Show Model\n\nA Lionel package may need three layers:\n\n## Shared media primitives\nVideo Source, Timed Media Segment, Transcript Segment, Topic, Person, Organization, Claim, and Source Document.\n\n## Lionel editorial vocabulary\nRecurring moves that survive comparison across episodes.\n\n## Episode-format templates\nPossible formats include Thesis Monologue, Media Reaction, Multi-topic Roundup, Response to Another Creator, and Interview or Guest Discussion.\n\nOne show template may therefore be a **package of node classes plus several composition templates**, not one rigid graph.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786052694504,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study-protocol",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Comparison Protocol",
      "root": false,
